MerkleAdapterLoss
├── when a queued withdrawal matures after a loss
│   ├── when the loss was accepted in the preceding report
│   │   └── it releases at most surviving authenticated NAV
│   ├── when the loss first appears at maturity
│   │   ├── when it exceeds the guard limit
│   │   │   └── it freezes without changing any withdrawal bucket
│   │   └── when the exact authenticated report is approved
│   │       └── it reserves surviving NAV and emits the remaining net NAV
│   ├── when no assets survive
│   │   └── it clears the matured request and permits subsequent reports
│   └── when the request exceeds NAV up to uint256.max
│       └── it caps the request before adding reserves without overflowing
├── given allocations or older withdrawal reserves
│   ├── it preserves pending allocations and already-matured withdrawals
│   ├── it settles consecutive withdrawal batches without a vault interaction
│   └── it reverts on stored-reserve overflow during delivery or review
├── when surviving NAV is not fully returned to the adapter
│   └── it freezes without treating temporary illiquidity as an additional loss
└── when settling a withdrawal bucket
    ├── it only permits the paired oracle to call
    └── it matures the surviving withdrawal and promotes deferred requests and allocations
